fullDescription.markdown:
MyBatis provider annotations (@SelectProvider, @InsertProvider, etc.) delegate
SQL generation to a Java method. If that method concatenates user input into
the SQL string, it is vulnerable to SQL injection.

Example (vulnerable):
```java
public class SqlProvider {
    public String findByName(String name) {
        return "SELECT * FROM users WHERE name = '" + name + "'";  // Injection!
    }
}

@SelectProvider(type = SqlProvider.class, method = "findByName")
User findByName(String name);
```

To remediate this issue:
- Use MyBatis SQL builder with proper parameterization
- Never concatenate user input into SQL strings
- Use #{...} parameter placeholders in the generated SQL

