Java EE web components (Servlets, Filters, Listeners) should not contain
main() methods in production code. The presence of a main() method typically
indicates:
- Debugging code left in production
- Testing code that should be in test classes
- Potential security exposure if the main method can be invoked

Example (problematic):
```java
public class MyServlet extends HttpServlet {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        // Debug code - should not be in production
    }

    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest req, HttpServletResponse resp) {
        // Normal servlet handling
    }
}
```

To remediate this issue:
- Remove main() methods from production Servlet/Filter/Listener classes
- Move debug/test code to separate test classes
- Use proper logging instead of System.out in main() for debugging

