LDAP simple authentication (username/password) over unencrypted connections exposes
credentials to interception. When using `ldap://` URLs with `SECURITY_AUTHENTICATION`
set to `simple`, credentials are transmitted in cleartext unless SSL/TLS is configured.

This rule detects LDAP configurations that:
1. Use plaintext `ldap://` protocol (not `ldaps://`)
2. Use simple authentication method
3. Do not explicitly configure SSL/TLS protection

### Vulnerable code example

```java
// BAD: Simple auth over unencrypted LDAP
Hashtable<String, String> env = new Hashtable<>();
env.put(Context.INITIAL_CONTEXT_FACTORY, "com.sun.jndi.ldap.LdapCtxFactory");
env.put(Context.PROVIDER_URL, "ldap://ldap.example.com:389");
env.put(Context.SECURITY_AUTHENTICATION, "simple");
env.put(Context.SECURITY_PRINCIPAL, "cn=admin,dc=example,dc=com");
env.put(Context.SECURITY_CREDENTIALS, password);
DirContext ctx = new InitialDirContext(env);
```

### Remediation

Option 1: Use LDAPS (LDAP over SSL):

```java
// GOOD: Use ldaps:// for encrypted connection
Hashtable<String, String> env = new Hashtable<>();
env.put(Context.INITIAL_CONTEXT_FACTORY, "com.sun.jndi.ldap.LdapCtxFactory");
env.put(Context.PROVIDER_URL, "ldaps://ldap.example.com:636");
env.put(Context.SECURITY_AUTHENTICATION, "simple");
env.put(Context.SECURITY_PRINCIPAL, "cn=admin,dc=example,dc=com");
env.put(Context.SECURITY_CREDENTIALS, password);
DirContext ctx = new InitialDirContext(env);
```

Option 2: Configure SSL explicitly:

```java
// GOOD: Configure SSL protocol
Hashtable<String, String> env = new Hashtable<>();
env.put(Context.INITIAL_CONTEXT_FACTORY, "com.sun.jndi.ldap.LdapCtxFactory");
env.put(Context.PROVIDER_URL, "ldap://ldap.example.com:389");
env.put(Context.SECURITY_AUTHENTICATION, "simple");
env.put(Context.SECURITY_PROTOCOL, "ssl");  // Enable SSL
env.put(Context.SECURITY_PRINCIPAL, "cn=admin,dc=example,dc=com");
env.put(Context.SECURITY_CREDENTIALS, password);
DirContext ctx = new InitialDirContext(env);
```

Additional recommendations:
- Prefer LDAPS (port 636) over StartTLS for simpler configuration
- Ensure LDAP server certificates are properly validated
- Consider using SASL mechanisms like GSSAPI/Kerberos for stronger authentication

